I did not implement the `last-input` recording. The node's `with` clause grants only `http-client`, `notifier` and `wall-clock`. Writing to a shared store needs a state interface such as `aap:caps/state-rw`, which would give the node authority it wasn't granted. To record the input, the node's `with` clause would first need a `StateHandle<'…', read-write>` added. The output is unchanged.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{heartbeat-report};

    import aap:caps/http-client@0.1.0;
    import aap:caps/notifier@0.1.0;
    import wasi:clocks/wall-clock@0.2.0;

    export run: func(feed-url: string) -> heartbeat-report;
}
```

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

use crate::aap::caps::{http_client, notifier};
use crate::wasi::clocks::wall_clock;

struct Node;

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(feed_url: String) -> HeartbeatReport {
        let seconds = wall_clock::now().seconds;
        let body = http_client::get(&feed_url);
        let fetched = body.chars().count() as u32;
        let notified = notifier::notify(&format!(
            "heartbeat at {}s: fetched {} characters from {}",
            seconds, fetched, feed_url
        ));
        HeartbeatReport {
            seconds,
            fetched,
            notified,
        }
    }
}

export!(Node);
```

